An add-on install script (one with "requires:", like Black Ops Cold War
on top of Battle.net) takes its Wine version from the game it requires.
FamiDrive sets that to "custom" (stores.nix), and get_wine_path() then
asks for the "custom" path with no config to read it from:
"Custom wine paths are only supported when a configuration is
available." Let "custom" fall through to the runner-config branch
below, which passes the config. Same code on Lutris master, 2026-10-14.

--- a/lutris/installer/commands.py
+++ b/lutris/installer/commands.py
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
         None if the wine exe can't be located."""
         runner = self.get_runner_class(self.installer.runner)()
         version = runner.get_installer_runner_version(self.installer, use_runner_config=False)
-        if version:
+        if version and version != "custom":
             wine_path = get_wine_path_for_version(version)
             return wine_path
 
